msgid "系统调用与 UAPI"
msgstr "System Calls and UAPI"

msgid "约定"
msgstr "Conventions"

msgid ""
"x86_64 使用 Linux syscall 编号与寄存器约定，未知接口返回 ENOSYS。 公开线协议位于 include/uapi，headers_install 由 "
"configs/header-export.list 控制；私有 task、页表和驱动状态不导出为用户 ABI。固定宽度、长度、版本、 边界和负 errno 都是接口契约的一部分。"
msgstr ""
"x86_64 uses Linux syscall numbers and register conventions; unknown interfaces return ENOSYS. "
"Public wire formats reside in include/uapi, and configs/header-export.list controls "
"headers_install. Private task, page-table, and driver state is not exported as a user ABI. Fixed "
"widths, lengths, versions, bounds, and negative errno values are all part of the interface "
"contract."

msgid "vDSO 的 ELF 符号版本、辅助向量、vvar 邻接映射及时间读取均有专用测试。 不支持的时钟或条件继续走真实 syscall，不返回猜测值。"
msgstr ""
"Dedicated tests cover vDSO ELF symbol versions, auxiliary vectors, adjacent vvar mappings, and "
"time reads. Unsupported clocks or conditions fall back to real syscalls rather than returning "
"guessed values."

msgid "兼容"
msgstr "Compatibility"

msgid ""
"公开头保留实际支持的兼容名称，旧用户库不能伪装成新 SONAME。 只实现的接口才可视为可用；头文件存在不能代替完整运行认证。 接口修改同步内核、导出头、用户态包装、消费者和必要验证，不以更新 "
"golden 替代布局或语义审查。"
msgstr ""
"Public headers retain compatibility names that are actually supported; old user libraries must not"
" masquerade as a new SONAME. Only implemented interfaces can be considered available; the presence"
" of a header does not establish full runtime certification. Interface changes must be synchronized"
" across the kernel, exported headers, userspace wrappers, consumers, and necessary validation. "
"Updating golden data does not replace layout or semantic review."

msgid "目录 bind mount"
msgstr "Directory Bind Mounts"

msgid ""
"``mount(source, target, NULL, MS_BIND, NULL)`` 支持非递归目录绑定。 新挂载保留源目录的实际 "
"inode、父链和文件系统生命周期，继承源挂载的 只读、nosuid、nodev 等策略。``/proc/self/mountinfo`` 的 "
"root 字段报告源目录 在文件系统内的路径；命名空间路径、``..`` 和 chroot 边界按新挂载计算。 "
"源文件系统在绑定仍存在时不能正常卸载，解绑不销毁源文件系统。"
msgstr ""
"``mount(source, target, NULL, MS_BIND, NULL)`` supports nonrecursive "
"directory binds. The new mount retains the source directory's actual "
"inode, parent chain, and filesystem lifecycle, and inherits source mount "
"policies such as read-only, nosuid, and nodev. The root field of "
"``/proc/self/mountinfo`` reports the source directory's path within its "
"filesystem; namespace paths, ``..``, and chroot boundaries are computed "
"relative to the new mount. The source filesystem cannot be ordinarily "
"unmounted while the bind remains, and unbinding does not destroy it."

msgid ""
"``MS_BIND | MS_REC`` 还会复制源目录下的挂载拓扑。子挂载在目的树中拥有新的 挂载 ID 和独立策略，但仍共享各自的源 "
"inode 和文件系统。源目录之外的挂载和 unbindable 子树不复制。准备失败时目的树和现有挂载保持原样。"
msgstr "``MS_BIND | MS_REC`` also copies the mount topology beneath the source directory. The new attachments have their own mount IDs and policies but share their respective source inodes and filesystems. Mounts outside the source directory and unbindable subtrees are skipped. Preparation failure leaves the destination tree and existing mounts unchanged."

msgid "``mount(NULL, target, NULL, MS_BIND | MS_REMOUNT | MS_RDONLY, NULL)`` 只更新目标挂载点的策略，不读取源、类型或文件系统选项。源挂载、子挂载和共享 文件系统保持原样。省略 atime 选项时保留原策略；共享文件系统只读时，清除 挂载点的只读标志不会使其可写。"
msgstr "``mount(NULL, target, NULL, MS_BIND | MS_REMOUNT | MS_RDONLY, NULL)`` only changes the policy at the target mountpoint. It does not read the source, type, or filesystem options. The source mount, submounts, and shared filesystem are unchanged. Omitted atime options preserve the existing policy. If the shared filesystem is read-only, clearing the mountpoint's read-only flag does not make it writable."

msgid "只读转换在目标挂载上仍有以写入模式打开的普通文件时返回 EBUSY，且不改变策略。 dup、fork 和文件映射持有的同一打开文件描述也会延续这项限制。其他挂载上的写者 或仅持有 O_PATH 不会阻止此转换。"
msgstr "A readonly transition returns EBUSY without changing policy while any regular file is open for writing on the target mount. References to the same open file description from dup, fork, and file mappings extend that restriction. Writers on other mounts and O_PATH-only handles do not block the transition."

msgid "文件绑定尚不支持，返回明确错误。"
msgstr "File binds are not yet supported and return an explicit error."


msgid "按任务选择 uname 系统名"
msgstr "Selecting the uname system name per task"

msgid "``<reliefos/prctl.h>`` 提供以下不需要特权的 ``prctl`` 扩展："
msgstr "``<reliefos/prctl.h>`` provides the following unprivileged ``prctl`` extensions:"

msgid "``RELIEFOS_PR_SET_UNAME_LINUX``（``0x52550001``）：arg2 为 0 或 1， 关闭或开启当前任务的 Linux 系统名；arg3、arg4、arg5 必须为零。"
msgstr "``RELIEFOS_PR_SET_UNAME_LINUX`` (``0x52550001``): arg2 is 0 or 1 to disable or enable the calling task's Linux system name; arg3, arg4, and arg5 must be zero."

msgid "``RELIEFOS_PR_GET_UNAME_LINUX``（``0x52550002``）：所有参数为零， 返回当前选择 0 或 1。"
msgstr "``RELIEFOS_PR_GET_UNAME_LINUX`` (``0x52550002``): all arguments must be zero; returns the current selection, 0 or 1."

msgid "非法值及非零保留参数返回 EINVAL，状态不变。新任务默认使用 ReliefNT； fork、vfork、clone 复制调用任务的选择，exec 保留选择。已经存在的其他任务 不受影响，线程也可独立设置该值。该开关仅将 ``uname(2)`` 返回的 ``sysname`` 改为 Linux，其余字段、全局 UTS 状态及 procfs 均不改变。 使用标准 libc prctl 包装或原始系统调用均可；不改变 personality 数值语义。"
msgstr "Invalid values and nonzero reserved arguments return EINVAL without changing state. New tasks use ReliefNT by default. fork, vfork, and clone copy the calling task's selection, and exec preserves it. Other existing tasks are unaffected; threads may also set their selection independently. The switch changes only the ``sysname`` returned by ``uname(2)`` to Linux; other fields, global UTS state, and procfs are unchanged. Both the standard libc prctl wrapper and raw syscalls are supported. Linux personality values retain their existing meaning."

msgid "私有和不可绑定挂载"
msgstr "Private and unbindable mounts"

msgid "新挂载默认是 private。``mount(NULL, target, NULL, MS_PRIVATE, NULL)`` 将 目标恢复为 private；``MS_UNBINDABLE`` 使目标不可作为 bind 源，并使递归 bind 跳过该子树。``MS_REC`` 将同一类型应用于目标及其现有子挂载；以后新建的子挂载 不会继承 unbindable。类型变更要求 ``CAP_SYS_ADMIN`` 且目标必须是挂载根， 不改变访问策略、文件系统状态或已有 bind。``/proc/self/mountinfo`` 使用 ``unbindable`` 可选字段报告不可绑定挂载。共享和 slave 传播尚不支持。"
msgstr "New mounts are private by default. ``mount(NULL, target, NULL, MS_PRIVATE, NULL)`` makes the target private again. ``MS_UNBINDABLE`` prohibits using the target as a bind source and prunes its subtree from recursive binds. ``MS_REC`` applies the selected type to the target and its existing submounts; new submounts do not inherit the unbindable type. Changing the type requires ``CAP_SYS_ADMIN`` and a target at a mount root. It does not change access policy, filesystem state, or existing binds. ``/proc/self/mountinfo`` reports the ``unbindable`` optional field. Shared and slave propagation are not yet supported."

msgid "延迟卸载"
msgstr "Lazy Unmount"

msgid "``umount2(target, MNT_DETACH)`` 立即移除目标挂载及其子挂载的命名空间连接， 不等待持有者或同步刷盘。新的路径查找会看到原挂载点下的内容，挂载表不再列出 已摘除的挂载。永久的命名空间基准根不可摘除。"
msgstr "``umount2(target, MNT_DETACH)`` immediately disconnects the target and its submounts from the namespace without waiting for references or synchronously flushing data. Fresh lookups see the original contents beneath the mountpoint, and the mount table no longer lists the detached mounts. The permanent namespace anchor cannot be detached."

msgid "已打开的文件及持有的目录仍可使用，子挂载的独立引用亦有效。从保留的目录开始 查找时不再跨越被摘除的挂载边，``..`` 不越过已摘除的挂载根。当工作目录不再 连接到任务根时，原始 ``getcwd`` 返回以 ``(unreachable)`` 开头的路径。 最后的引用释放后由 VFS 工作队列完成文件系统清理。"
msgstr "Open files and retained directories remain usable, including independent references to submounts. Lookups starting from a retained directory no longer cross the detached mount edges, and ``..`` stops at the detached mount root. If the working directory is no longer connected to the task root, raw ``getcwd`` returns a path prefixed with ``(unreachable)``. The VFS work queue completes filesystem cleanup after the last reference is released."

msgid "glibc 线程与 CPU 状态兼容"
msgstr "glibc thread and CPU-state compatibility"

msgid ""
"以下行为按 x86_64 Linux ABI 实现。``rseq``、futex PI 操作和扩展信号帧使用 Linux 的接口及布局。POSIX 线程、互斥锁和 CPU "
"时间接口由用户态 libc 提供。"
msgstr ""
"The following behavior implements the x86_64 Linux ABI. ``rseq``, futex PI operations, and "
"extended signal frames use Linux interfaces and layouts. Userspace libc provides the POSIX "
"thread, mutex, and CPU-time interfaces."

msgid "rseq"
msgstr "rseq"

msgid ""
"注册后向用户区域发布实际运行 CPU，线程迁移后在返回用户态前更新 ``cpu_id_start``、``cpu_id``、``node_id`` 和 ``mm_cid``。当前 "
"NUMA 节点为 0， ``mm_cid`` 使用执行 CPU 的逻辑索引。抢占或信号中断活动临界区时，内核验证 描述符、地址范围及 abort 签名，清除 "
"``rseq_cs``，并跳转至 abort 地址。 无效描述符或不可访问的注册区域触发同步 SIGSEGV。"
msgstr ""
"Registration publishes the actual execution CPU to the userspace area. After thread "
"migration, ``cpu_id_start``, ``cpu_id``, ``node_id``, and ``mm_cid`` are updated before "
"returning to userspace. The current NUMA node is 0, and ``mm_cid`` uses the logical index of "
"the execution CPU. When preemption or a signal interrupts an active critical section, the "
"kernel validates the descriptor, address ranges, and abort signature, clears ``rseq_cs``, and"
" jumps to the abort address. An invalid descriptor or inaccessible registered area triggers a"
" synchronous SIGSEGV."

msgid ""
"``fork`` 复制注册信息，共享地址空间的新线程独立注册，``exec`` 清除注册。 注册保留用户提供的临界区指针及 flags。glibc 可直接读取其 TLS rseq 区域以"
" 实现 ``sched_getcpu``，并可按其自身配置关闭 rseq 使用。"
msgstr ""
"``fork`` copies the registration. New threads sharing the address space register "
"independently, and ``exec`` clears the registration. Registration preserves the critical-"
"section pointer and flags supplied by userspace. glibc can read its TLS rseq area directly to"
" implement ``sched_getcpu``, and can disable rseq use through its own configuration."

msgid "PI futex"
msgstr "PI futex"

msgid ""
"实现 ``FUTEX_LOCK_PI``、``FUTEX_TRYLOCK_PI``、``FUTEX_UNLOCK_PI`` 和 ``FUTEX_LOCK_PI2``，支持私有及共享 "
"futex、竞争交接、死锁检查、超时和 robust owner death。共享等待队列保留物理页，退出时释放等待关系。 普通 futex 与 PI 等待队列混用返回 EINVAL。"
msgstr ""
"``FUTEX_LOCK_PI``, ``FUTEX_TRYLOCK_PI``, ``FUTEX_UNLOCK_PI``, and ``FUTEX_LOCK_PI2`` are "
"implemented with support for private and shared futexes, contended handoff, deadlock checks, "
"timeouts, and robust owner death. Shared wait queues retain physical pages, and exit releases"
" wait relationships. Mixing ordinary futex and PI wait queues returns EINVAL."

msgid ""
"``LOCK_PI`` 使用绝对 CLOCK_REALTIME 超时。``LOCK_PI2`` 默认使用绝对 CLOCK_MONOTONIC，可通过 "
"``FUTEX_CLOCK_REALTIME`` 选择实时钟。 PI 等待被信号打断后按 Linux 规则重启，包括未设置 ``SA_RESTART`` 的处理器。 "
"已完成的锁所有权交接先结束该次等待，再交付待处理信号。"
msgstr ""
"``LOCK_PI`` uses an absolute CLOCK_REALTIME timeout. ``LOCK_PI2`` defaults to absolute "
"CLOCK_MONOTONIC time and can select the realtime clock with ``FUTEX_CLOCK_REALTIME``. Signal-"
"interrupted PI waits restart according to Linux rules, including handlers without "
"``SA_RESTART``. A completed lock-ownership handoff finishes the wait before delivering "
"pending signals."

msgid ""
"当前调度器仅接纳 SCHED_OTHER，PI 队列按相同有效优先级的 FIFO 顺序交接。 SCHED_FIFO、SCHED_RR 的实时调度与优先级提升仍需对应调度策略支持。 "
"``FUTEX_WAIT_REQUEUE_PI`` 和 ``FUTEX_CMP_REQUEUE_PI`` 尚未实现，返回 ENOSYS。"
msgstr ""
"The current scheduler accepts only SCHED_OTHER. PI queues hand off ownership in FIFO order "
"among tasks with equal effective priority. Realtime scheduling and priority boosting for "
"SCHED_FIFO and SCHED_RR still require support for those scheduling policies. "
"``FUTEX_WAIT_REQUEUE_PI`` and ``FUTEX_CMP_REQUEUE_PI`` are not yet implemented and return "
"ENOSYS."

msgid "CPU 时间时钟"
msgstr "CPU-time clocks"

msgid ""
"除当前进程和线程的固定 clock ID 外，支持 Linux 编码的进程及线程 CPU 时钟， 供 ``clock_getcpuclockid`` 和 "
"``pthread_getcpuclockid`` 使用。PROF 和 SCHED 报告用户态与内核态累计时间，VIRT 报告用户态时间。进程时钟汇总线程组。 线程目标遵守 Linux "
"的线程组限制。``clock_gettime`` 和 ``clock_getres`` 按各自的目标验证规则处理编码 ID，非法 ID 返回 EINVAL。 当前时间统计及报告分辨率为 "
"10 ms。"
msgstr ""
"In addition to the fixed clock IDs for the current process and thread, Linux-encoded process "
"and thread CPU clocks are supported for ``clock_getcpuclockid`` and "
"``pthread_getcpuclockid``. PROF and SCHED report accumulated userspace and kernel time, while"
" VIRT reports userspace time. Process clocks aggregate the thread group. Thread targets obey "
"Linux thread-group restrictions. ``clock_gettime`` and ``clock_getres`` handle encoded IDs "
"according to their respective target-validation rules, returning EINVAL for invalid IDs. The "
"current accounting and reported resolution is 10 ms."

msgid "XSAVE 与信号帧"
msgstr "XSAVE and signal frames"

msgid ""
"支持 AVX 的 CPU 启用统一的 x87、SSE、AVX XSAVE 状态，任务保存区保持 64 字节对齐，调度切换保留全部启用状态。缺少所需 CPU 能力时使用 512 字节 "
"FXSAVE 状态。当前 XSAVE mask 为 0x7，保存区为 832 字节。"
msgstr ""
"CPUs supporting AVX enable a unified x87, SSE, and AVX XSAVE state. Task save areas remain "
"64-byte aligned, and scheduling switches preserve all enabled state. CPUs lacking the "
"required capabilities use a 512-byte FXSAVE state. The current XSAVE mask is 0x7, with an "
"832-byte save area."

msgid ""
"信号帧包含 Linux 的 ``_fpx_sw_bytes``、XSAVE bitmap 和末尾 magic。 ``rt_sigreturn`` 验证对齐、长度、feature "
"位、保留字段和 MXCSR，并恢复 x87、SSE、YMM 状态。传统 fpstate 及空 fpstate 按其 Linux 语义处理。"
msgstr ""
"Signal frames contain Linux ``_fpx_sw_bytes``, an XSAVE bitmap, and a trailing magic value. "
"``rt_sigreturn`` validates alignment, lengths, feature bits, reserved fields, and MXCSR, then"
" restores x87, SSE, and YMM state. Legacy fpstate and null fpstate follow their Linux "
"semantics."

msgid "定向验证"
msgstr "Targeted validation"

msgid ""
"``tools/test_linux_threads.py`` 覆盖 rseq 生命周期、PI 等待队列与信号恢复。 CPU accounting 和用户态返回路径另有宿主回归测试。 "
"``tools/tests/glibc_runtime_probe.c`` 可由原版 glibc 工具链编译，覆盖 编码 CPU 时钟、rseq 迁移与临界区中断、PI mutex "
"竞争、信号、双时钟超时、 robust 恢复、AVX 调度切换和扩展信号帧。"
msgstr ""
"``tools/test_linux_threads.py`` covers the rseq lifecycle, PI wait queues, and signal "
"restoration. CPU accounting and userspace return paths have additional host regression tests."
" ``tools/tests/glibc_runtime_probe.c`` can be compiled with an unmodified glibc toolchain and"
" covers encoded CPU clocks, rseq migration and critical-section interruption, PI mutex "
"contention, signals, timeouts with both clocks, robust recovery, AVX scheduling switches, and"
" extended signal frames."

msgid ""
"此次使用未修改的 Debian glibc 2.41，在双核 QEMU/KVM 中分别验证启用 AVX/XSAVE 和关闭 AVX/XSAVE 的 CPU 配置。动态 "
"ELF、pthread/TLS、 ``posix_spawn``、``dlopen/dlsym``、localhost NSS 和普通 robust mutex 也已运行。关闭 AVX "
"时跳过 AVX 专项。该覆盖范围以外的应用及 glibc 版本 仍需各自验证。VMware 验证未完成，实体硬件未验证。"
msgstr ""
"This validation used unmodified Debian glibc 2.41 on dual-core QEMU/KVM with CPU "
"configurations enabling and disabling AVX/XSAVE. Dynamic ELF, pthread/TLS, ``posix_spawn``, "
"``dlopen/dlsym``, localhost NSS, and ordinary robust mutexes were also exercised. AVX-"
"specific checks are skipped when AVX is disabled. Applications and glibc versions outside "
"this coverage still require individual validation. VMware validation is incomplete, and "
"physical hardware has not been validated."
